# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
!testdata/golden/**/*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
AGENTS.md
# CLAUDE.md
test*.sg
tmp*.sg
.cursor/
build/
target/
# A test project TestCrossingBackendGuardsCoverImportedModules builds in its own
# package directory (module resolution is relative to it). A process killed
# mid-gate leaves it behind; ignored so a leftover cannot dirty a SHA-pinned
# worktree and make the heavy-run guard refuse every later run of a count.
internal/buildpipeline/rv2-crossing-xmod-*/

# Surge project
helloworld/
surgesqlite/
neon/
sigil/
schess/
surgekv/
scribe/
skvc/

surge
!cmd/surge
!stdlib/directives/test/test.sg

*.o

.security-key
.claude-flow/
.serena/
.swarm/
.vds_creds
